<title>POLAND: ALL POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FALL. [CORRECTED 14:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>ALL POLISH MINIMUM T-BILL PRICES FALL. [CORRECTED 14:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline and throughout to read &quot;all&quot; rather than &quot;most&quot; prices fall.)</p>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish</p>
<p>T-bills fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 527</p>
<p>million zlotys against a 1.1 billion zloty offer, the finance</p>
<p>ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold T-bills worth 273 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Poland will offer 1.1 billion zlotys worth of bills at its</p>
<p>next primary tender on Monday, August 18.</p>
<p> T-bill	     8-week   13-week   26-week   52-week</p>
<p> new min price    96.60     94.58     89.66     81.21</p>
<p> (pvs auction)   (96.63)   (94.64)   (89.80)   (81.47)</p>
<p> new max price    96.72     94.96     89.99     81.54</p>
<p> (pvs auction)   (96.77)   (94.82)   (89.96)   (81.60)</p>
<p> offer	     200.0     200.0     200.0     500.0</p>
<p> bids recorded   236.3     116.3	45.0     129.0</p>
<p> bids accepted    88.5	58.8	37.9	87.6</p>
<p> next auction    200.0     200.0     200.0     500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
